From: William Mangum <william@wsds.io>
Subject: [PATCH] the built-in table names no file

psl-make-dafsa writes the path of the list it read into the table it
generates, and the library keeps it as _psl_filename: psl_builtin_filename()
returns it, and psl_builtin_outdated() and psl_latest() stat it at run time
to see whether a newer list lies there. A distribution passes the path of its
installed list. A cross build has no such path: the list is the one in the
source tree, so the table carries the full path of the build directory, which
names the builder and exists on no machine the library runs on.

The name is written empty, which is the value the library has without
built-in data and the one value that makes it stat nothing: a relative or an
invented path would be a place where a file could be put for it to load.

Upstream: not submitted (the name is by design there; embraOS carries this).
Signed-off-by: William Mangum <william@wsds.io>
---
--- a/src/psl-make-dafsa
+++ b/src/psl-make-dafsa
@@ -518,7 +518,7 @@
   text += b'static int _psl_nexceptions = %d;\n' % psl_nexceptions
   text += b'static int _psl_nwildcards = %d;\n' % psl_nwildcards
   text += b'static const char _psl_sha1_checksum[] = "%s";\n' % bytes(sha1_file(psl_input_file), **codecs)
-  text += b'static const char _psl_filename[] = "%s";\n' % bytes(psl_input_file, **codecs)
+  text += b'static const char _psl_filename[] = "";\n'
   return text

 def words_to_whatever(words, converter, utf_mode, codecs):
